---
// Accessibility statement (BremBGG / BITV 2.0), after the University of Bremen's own statement
// (https://www.uni-bremen.de/en/accessibility): its structure and fixed wording (introduction,
// reporting barriers, enforcement) are taken over; status, barriers and method describe this
// site. Decided by Martin (November 2026): English, "partially compliant" (no independent BITV
// test yet), four known barriers, reports to the lab email. Update the date when the site's
// accessibility changes or a test is done.
import LegalPage from '../layouts/LegalPage.astro';
import { site, contactEmail } from '../lib/site';
import { DEFAULT_SITE_URL } from '../lib/site-url';

const siteUrl = new URL(Astro.site ?? DEFAULT_SITE_URL).hostname;
---

<LegalPage
  title="Accessibility statement"
  lead="How accessible this website is, and how to report barriers"
  lang="en"
>
  <p>
    We strive to make this website accessible. The declaration of accessibility is required by the
    Bremen Equal Opportunities for Disabled Persons Act (BremBGG). The technical requirements for
    accessibility are derived from the Barrier-Free Information Technology Ordinance (BITV 2.0).
    This declaration on digital accessibility applies to the website of the {site.name} (
    {site.short}), {siteUrl}.
  </p>

  <h2>How accessible is the site?</h2>
  <p>
    This website is partially compliant with the requirements of BITV 2.0. It was designed to meet
    the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1 at level AA, on which BITV 2.0 is based: it
    can be used by keyboard, has visible focus, text alternatives for images and sufficient colour
    contrast, and it respects the setting for reduced motion. It has not yet been tested by an
    independent body. The exceptions known to us are listed below.
  </p>

  <h2>Which areas are not barrier-free?</h2>

  <h3>1. Easy German and German Sign Language</h3>
  <p>
    a) Description: This website has no explanations in Easy German (Leichte Sprache) or German Sign
    Language.
  </p>
  <p>
    b) Measures: The University of Bremen provides its{' '}
    <a
      href="https://www.uni-bremen.de/erklaerung-zur-barrierefreiheit-in-leichter-sprache"
      lang="de"
    >
      declaration of accessibility in Easy German
    </a>
    .
  </p>

  <h3>2. Videos</h3>
  <p>
    a) Description: Videos are embedded from YouTube. Whether they have subtitles depends on the
    video.
  </p>
  <p>
    b) Measures: Each video can also be opened directly on YouTube, where available subtitles and
    transcripts can be used.
  </p>

  <h3>3. External documents</h3>
  <p>
    a) Description: Papers, slides and other documents linked from this website are published by
    other providers (for example publishers, arXiv or Zenodo). We cannot ensure their accessibility.
  </p>
  <p>b) Measures: If you need content in an accessible form, please contact us (see below).</p>

  <h3>4. Interactive demos and the research map</h3>
  <p>
    a) Description: The course demos and the research map are visual and interactive. They can be
    operated by keyboard, but screen readers may not convey everything they show.
  </p>
  <p>
    b) Measures: Each demo page explains in text what the demo shows. The research themes of each
    member are also listed as text on their profile.
  </p>

  <h2>When and how was the declaration of accessibility created?</h2>
  <p>
    This declaration was created on 17 November 2026. It is based on a self-assessment: whenever the
    website changes, every page is checked automatically for accessibility problems (with axe-core)
    at desktop and phone widths, and the interactive parts are tested for keyboard use.
  </p>

  <h2>Do you want to report barriers?</h2>
  <p>
    We would like to further improve our services. Feel free to share your digital accessibility
    issues and questions with us via email at{' '}
    {contactEmail ? (
      <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>
    ) : (
      <span class="ph">[lab email]</span>
    )}
    . If we cannot resolve your concern, you can then turn to Bremen's{' '}
    <a href="https://www.behindertenbeauftragter.bremen.de/der-beauftragte/zentralstelle-fuer-barrierefreie-informationstechnik-28011">
      Central Office for Accessible Information Technology
    </a>
    , which also provides information on the enforcement procedure.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
